\name{cellucid_analysis_signature_get}
\alias{cellucid_analysis_signature_get}
\title{Read gene signature options}
\usage{
cellucid_analysis_signature_get(viewer, in_ = "panel")
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{in_}{Either exactly \code{"panel"} (The Analysis panel); or a whole number (at least 1) (A floating analysis window, by its number (1 is the first open)). Default \code{"panel"}, the viewer's own. Sent as the parameter \code{in}.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{analysis}, \code{computed_on} (What the result was computed on), \code{has_result}, \code{in}, \code{options}, \code{pages}, \code{running}, \code{stale} (The result no longer matches its inputs (the reasons say what changed)), \code{stale_reasons}. Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
The gene signature analysis's options, pages and result state.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{analysis.signature.get} (Analysis). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
